          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_FC0B77A4_CONCEPTS_01",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR__FC0B77A4_1",
          "title": "1. Key Academic Principles: Bohr Model of Hydrogen Atom, Quantized Radii and Energy Levels",
          "contentMarkdown": "In the Bohr model of the hydrogen atom, electron angular momentum is quantized in circular orbits: m_e * v * r = n * h / (2*pi), where n = 1, 2, 3... Radii of stationary Bohr orbits in hydrogenic species are given by r_n = a_0 * n^2 / Z, where a_0 = 52.9 pm.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_FC0B77A4_F877C487",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_FC0B77A4_88F6993E"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_FC0B77A4_CONCEPTS_02",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR__FC0B77A4_2",
          "title": "2. Key Academic Principles: Bohr Model of Hydrogen Atom, Quantized Radii and Energy Levels",
          "contentMarkdown": "Energy of stationary states in hydrogenic species is quantized as E_n = - 2.18 x 10^-18 J * (Z^2 / n^2) = - 13.6 eV * (Z^2 / n^2). Stationary states: Electron does not radiate energy while in a permissible orbit.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_FC0B77A4_DC58614C",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_CHE_FC0B77A4_0F4C8566"
